**`rust/src/lib.rs`** — added `filter_by_tag`:
```rust
pub fn filter_by_tag<'a>(notes: &'a [Note], tag: &str) -> Vec<&'a Note> {
    notes
        .iter()
        .filter(|n| n.tags.iter().any(|t| t == tag))
        .collect()
}
```
- Exact match on each note's `tags` vector (via `any`), preserving input order.

**`rust/src/main.rs`** — wired `--tag <TAG>` into the `list` command:
- Parses `--tag <value>` from the remaining CLI arguments after the subcommand.
- When present, calls `filter_by_tag` and prints only matching notes.
- When absent, prints all notes (unchanged behavior).


